[[:db/retract 17592186160970 :answer-field/choices 17592186160975] {:db/id 17592186115249 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4527164d-e7cb-52d0-bbe2-36d132296780"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4527164d-e7cb-52d0-bbe2-36d132296780" :question/id #uuid "4527164d-e7cb-52d0-bbe2-36d132296780" :question/math-academy-id "q-132004" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $N$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to the blank spaces?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[N\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $N$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $N$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[N\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}↔\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${N}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{N}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b9000ab-e8bd-5f5c-84a8-8cef429e6f0b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b9000ab-e8bd-5f5c-84a8-8cef429e6f0b" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b9000ab-e8bd-5f5c-84a8-8cef429e6f0b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bf0407bf-4311-58c0-b114-98ed3e8ee02a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bf0407bf-4311-58c0-b114-98ed3e8ee02a" "answer-f5ac1651-aac3-521c-a66f-1cec99bd6d5a" "answer-1d53923c-6f45-51dc-ae6c-80093cc282ad" "answer-b5d7da9d-5400-5cbe-862a-032387dd245d" "answer-5d6c20a2-6c34-50ec-a6f8-5f88f21271d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bf0407bf-4311-58c0-b114-98ed3e8ee02a" :answer/id #uuid "bf0407bf-4311-58c0-b114-98ed3e8ee02a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f5ac1651-aac3-521c-a66f-1cec99bd6d5a" :answer/id #uuid "f5ac1651-aac3-521c-a66f-1cec99bd6d5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1d53923c-6f45-51dc-ae6c-80093cc282ad" :answer/id #uuid "1d53923c-6f45-51dc-ae6c-80093cc282ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b5d7da9d-5400-5cbe-862a-032387dd245d" :answer/id #uuid "b5d7da9d-5400-5cbe-862a-032387dd245d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5d6c20a2-6c34-50ec-a6f8-5f88f21271d9" :answer/id #uuid "5d6c20a2-6c34-50ec-a6f8-5f88f21271d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186304939 :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\nI. ${y}^{′}+7xy=5$\n\nII. ${y}^{′}+7xy=0$\n\nIII. ${y}^{′}+7xy=-2y$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172093 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fba38d94-94f1-5e40-9342-c81f8eabc355"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-fba38d94-94f1-5e40-9342-c81f8eabc355" :question/id #uuid "fba38d94-94f1-5e40-9342-c81f8eabc355" :question/math-academy-id "q-124296" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=6u+4v+2,\\,y=5v-1\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 & a \\\\ 0 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6u+4v+2 \\\\ 5v-1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+4v+2 \\\\ 5v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u+4v \\\\ 5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}6 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=4+5+(-1)=8.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3d3eb90b-b341-501f-a49e-f9c67d7e1ee8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3d3eb90b-b341-501f-a49e-f9c67d7e1ee8" :answer-field/id #uuid "3d3eb90b-b341-501f-a49e-f9c67d7e1ee8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a0d4331d-d76a-550e-af61-65f77866dcfa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6bf5a0c1-0205-502f-9cbc-8cd0d9139fcc" "answer-5ec2e130-ad0b-5d90-874b-cafee34e58c7" "answer-dcc4abca-dbd0-5a8c-8460-f14372be7eed" "answer-a0d4331d-d76a-550e-af61-65f77866dcfa" "answer-d090baef-9223-53ba-b7a5-e64a993a1878"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6bf5a0c1-0205-502f-9cbc-8cd0d9139fcc" :answer/id #uuid "6bf5a0c1-0205-502f-9cbc-8cd0d9139fcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ec2e130-ad0b-5d90-874b-cafee34e58c7" :answer/id #uuid "5ec2e130-ad0b-5d90-874b-cafee34e58c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dcc4abca-dbd0-5a8c-8460-f14372be7eed" :answer/id #uuid "dcc4abca-dbd0-5a8c-8460-f14372be7eed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0d4331d-d76a-550e-af61-65f77866dcfa" :answer/id #uuid "a0d4331d-d76a-550e-af61-65f77866dcfa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d090baef-9223-53ba-b7a5-e64a993a1878" :answer/id #uuid "d090baef-9223-53ba-b7a5-e64a993a1878" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186124499 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-8744c31a-0769-5670-8154-7878dd8f3f11"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-8744c31a-0769-5670-8154-7878dd8f3f11" :question/id #uuid "8744c31a-0769-5670-8154-7878dd8f3f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-70713" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t-2 \\\\ y=2-3t \\\\ z=2t-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}t-2 \\\\ 2-3t \\\\ 2t-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\,2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-2,2,-1)$  and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9fdab432-8653-5165-9ae6-72fb1a348731"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9fdab432-8653-5165-9ae6-72fb1a348731" :answer-field/id #uuid "9fdab432-8653-5165-9ae6-72fb1a348731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-519e2e68-d953-5a17-b243-f7d7baf0d48c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a026363f-0997-50ef-819e-7238a42e62f8" "answer-ad9d7702-93e0-58b6-a557-5d52deb4131f" "answer-5a986f85-269d-547a-a60f-07e7c95d8225" "answer-519e2e68-d953-5a17-b243-f7d7baf0d48c" "answer-313bb2ba-1cbe-5a55-988a-686dd9f3cfca"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a026363f-0997-50ef-819e-7238a42e62f8" :answer/id #uuid "a026363f-0997-50ef-819e-7238a42e62f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad9d7702-93e0-58b6-a557-5d52deb4131f" :answer/id #uuid "ad9d7702-93e0-58b6-a557-5d52deb4131f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5a986f85-269d-547a-a60f-07e7c95d8225" :answer/id #uuid "5a986f85-269d-547a-a60f-07e7c95d8225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-519e2e68-d953-5a17-b243-f7d7baf0d48c" :answer/id #uuid "519e2e68-d953-5a17-b243-f7d7baf0d48c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-313bb2ba-1cbe-5a55-988a-686dd9f3cfca" :answer/id #uuid "313bb2ba-1cbe-5a55-988a-686dd9f3cfca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186162613 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 8 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${q}_{12}\\ne {q}_{21},$ we obtain $Q\\ne {Q}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186160970 :answer-field/correct 17592186160973 :answer-field/choices ["answer-a1875ce6-b60f-545c-9f54-6753f8dd61d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a1875ce6-b60f-545c-9f54-6753f8dd61d3" :answer/id #uuid "a1875ce6-b60f-545c-9f54-6753f8dd61d3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P,$ $Q,$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-bb107373-be8d-5258-84bf-9e57da002e0b" :activity/id #uuid "bb107373-be8d-5258-84bf-9e57da002e0b" :activity/title "Quiz 7" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-884993c3-99cd-577a-a81b-70f4ff6e9717" "step-227e9481-f504-5749-ab7b-6ee925602a24" "step-16085287-bd7c-5cbe-86ad-7e35c6ecbe2d" "step-41a93acd-03da-528e-886b-27d891c81a31" "step-e291609d-e0c6-5a4f-9e64-8be5c7b23f06" "step-812e19f7-331d-56a6-9f4e-7ad382b96943" "step-9165f4d4-1c48-5971-b376-5ef4c8b1c873" "step-0e975a13-b456-5602-b4a4-86ab4d7bf99f"] :activity/first-step "step-884993c3-99cd-577a-a81b-70f4ff6e9717" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-884993c3-99cd-577a-a81b-70f4ff6e9717" :step/id #uuid "884993c3-99cd-577a-a81b-70f4ff6e9717" :step/content "question-4527164d-e7cb-52d0-bbe2-36d132296780" :step/next "step-227e9481-f504-5749-ab7b-6ee925602a24" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-227e9481-f504-5749-ab7b-6ee925602a24" :step/id #uuid "227e9481-f504-5749-ab7b-6ee925602a24" :step/content 17592186304939 :step/next "step-16085287-bd7c-5cbe-86ad-7e35c6ecbe2d" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-16085287-bd7c-5cbe-86ad-7e35c6ecbe2d" :step/id #uuid "16085287-bd7c-5cbe-86ad-7e35c6ecbe2d" :step/content "question-fba38d94-94f1-5e40-9342-c81f8eabc355" :step/next "step-41a93acd-03da-528e-886b-27d891c81a31" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-41a93acd-03da-528e-886b-27d891c81a31" :step/id #uuid "41a93acd-03da-528e-886b-27d891c81a31" :step/content "question-8744c31a-0769-5670-8154-7878dd8f3f11" :step/next "step-e291609d-e0c6-5a4f-9e64-8be5c7b23f06" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-e291609d-e0c6-5a4f-9e64-8be5c7b23f06" :step/id #uuid "e291609d-e0c6-5a4f-9e64-8be5c7b23f06" :step/content 17592186275237 :step/next "step-812e19f7-331d-56a6-9f4e-7ad382b96943" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-812e19f7-331d-56a6-9f4e-7ad382b96943" :step/id #uuid "812e19f7-331d-56a6-9f4e-7ad382b96943" :step/content 17592